   "file": "Research/Arguments/Argument - Does ADHD medication change long-term outcomes.md"
  },
  {
   "id": "question",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 120,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 150,
   "color": "2",
   "text": "### Question<br><br>Do short-term symptom gains translate into long-term function, quality of life and safety?"
  },
  {
   "id": "deciding",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 460,
   "y": 120,
   "width": 400,
   "height": 170,
   "color": "6",
   "text": "### Evidence that would decide<br><br>Randomised long-term trials where feasible, and large prospective cohorts that record treatment exposure, functional outcomes and harms with pre-specified confounding control."
  },
  {
   "id": "guard",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 920,
   "y": 120,
   "width": 340,
   "height": 170,
   "color": "2",
   "text": "### Overreach guard<br><br>A symptom average is not a life outcome, and an absence of long-term evidence is not evidence of absence."
  },
  {
   "id": "legend",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -60,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 160,
   "color": "5",
   "text": "### Legend<br><br>Green: support for the framing.<br>Orange: tension or counter-evidence.<br>Purple: deciding evidence and hypotheses.<br>Edges label the relationship, not proof."
  },
  {
